questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot service experiences random worker threads hanging at 100% CPU utilization. Thread dumps reveal multiple threads executing inside `java.util.LinkedHashMap.get()`. The team uses a custom bounded cache implemented as follows:

java
@Component
public class UserSessionCache {
    private final Map<String, UserSession> cache = 
        new LinkedHashMap<String, UserSession>(1024, 0.75f, true) {
            @Override
            protected boolean removeEldestEntry(Map.Entry<String, UserSession> eldest) {
                return size() > 1000;
            }
        };

    public UserSession getSession(String id) {
        return cache.get(id);
    }

    public synchronized void putSession(String id, UserSession session) {
        cache.put(id, session);
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue in an e-commerce application. A Spring `@Service` manages order lines within a `@Transactional` method using a custom domain collection backed by a `HashSet<OrderLine>`. The entity defines `equals()` and `hashCode()` using its database-generated primary key:

java
@Entity
public class OrderLine {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;
    private String sku;

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (!(o instanceof OrderLine that)) return false;
        return id != null && Objects.equals(id, that.id);
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return Objects.hash(id);
    }
}


Inside a transactional method, transient `OrderLine` instances are added to a `HashSet<OrderLine>`, the parent order is saved via `entityManager.persist()`, and `entityManager.flush()` executes. Later in the same method, `orderLineSet.contains(line)` returns `false` for entities explicitly added to the set.

You are debugging a production issue where a microservice using dynamic Spring AOP advice steadily leaks memory, eventually crashing with `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Metaspace` followed by heap exhaustion. A heap dump shows millions of `Class<?>` instances and their corresponding `ClassLoader` instances retained through a custom reflection cache:

java
@Component
public class InvocationMetadataRegistry {
    private final Map<Class<?>, InvocationMetadata> metadataCache = new WeakHashMap<>();

    public void register(Class<?> targetClass, Method method) {
        metadataCache.put(targetClass, new InvocationMetadata(targetClass, method));
    }
}

class InvocationMetadata {
    private final Class<?> clazz;
    private final Method method;

    public InvocationMetadata(Class<?> clazz, Method method) {
        this.clazz = clazz;
        this.method = method;
    }
}
